14.11 Renewal Options

This policy is issued on a twelve-month basis and shall expire on July 1, 2027, unless cancelled or non-renewed. The insured may request renewal of this policy by submitting a written renewal application to the producer at least sixty (60) days prior to expiration. Renewal of this policy shall be at the sole discretion of Granite Shield Casualty Company, and all renewal terms, rates, conditions, and limits shall be subject to the underwriting requirements and practices of the insurer at the time of renewal.

14.12 Bankruptcy

If the named insured becomes subject to bankruptcy, insolvency proceedings, or receivership, this policy shall not be discharged or diminished by such proceedings, and the insurer shall remain obligated to pay covered claims in accordance with the terms of this policy.

14.13 Subrogation and Recovery

Except as waived in accordance with Section 11 above, Granite Shield Casualty Company shall have the right of subrogation against any person or entity responsible for any loss or damage covered under this policy. The named insured shall cooperate with the insurer in pursuing any subrogation rights and shall not execute any release or agreement that would impair such rights without the insurer's written consent. The insurer shall be subrogated to any and all recovery rights to the extent of any payment made for covered losses.

14.14 Governing Law

This policy shall be construed and governed in accordance with the laws and regulations of the State of Colorado, except that all provisions relative to the authority, duties, and obligations of the insurer shall be governed by the laws of the State of Iowa, the state in which the insurer is incorporated and domiciled. Any legal action arising under this policy shall be brought exclusively in the federal or state courts located in Denver, Colorado, provided that the insurer consents to such jurisdiction.

14.15 Conformity with Statute

All terms and provisions of this policy shall be subject to the insurance laws and regulations of each state in which the named insured conducts business. To the extent any provision of this policy conflicts with mandatory requirements of state law, the statutory requirement shall control.

